From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:32:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: throw away, menu and keys for the screenshot thumbnail

Throwing the thumbnail toward the right edge of the screen dismisses it at
once, and the dragged picture carries on the way it was thrown. A throw
is a drag that no app took, ending at least 40 px right of where it began,
mostly level, whose fastest 24 ms stretch in its last 150 ms of movement
reached 0.6 px/ms, and that did not rest before the release (a pointer
thrown into the edge may rest there briefly). A short or slow drag springs
back, and dropping onto an app still delivers the file.

Right-clicking it (or Shift+F10 or the Menu key) opens a menu: Open; Open
With, the default application first, then the others for the type and
Other Application... (the portal's chooser); Copy (the image; recordings
omit it); Copy File; Show in Filer; Rename..., which edits the name in
place; and Move to Trash, after which the thumbnail becomes a pill with
Undo for six seconds. The thumbnail stays while its menu is open, while it
is renamed and while it has keyboard focus.

Keys: Delete moves it to the Trash, Escape dismisses it, Enter opens it.
It joins Ctrl+Alt+Tab. Every action is logged under [luma-capture].
